{"title":"2025 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alice and Bazza are playing the <i>inekoalaty</i> game, a two‑player game whose rules depend on a positive real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> which is known to both players. On the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th turn of the game (starting with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />) the following happens:\n</p>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, Alice chooses a nonnegative real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/4/4c41ca6af2f7176a649464a9b887ac34496acf78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 + x_2 + \\cdots + x_n \\le \\lambda n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"17\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even, Bazza chooses a nonnegative real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e05ea0a197b2ea269ea4ffc7c15308795b2ce359.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1^2 + x_2^2 + \\cdots + x_n^2 \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"21\" /></li></ul>\n<p>If a player cannot choose a suitable <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, the game ends and the other player wins. If the game goes on forever, neither player wins. All chosen numbers are known to both players.\n</p><p>Determine all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> for which Alice has a winning strategy and all those for which Bazza has a winning strategy.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution\">Video solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/laYxMrfbsPE\">https://youtu.be/laYxMrfbsPE</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Lemma 1:</b> Alice can win if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/2/6f298794682c93d4c49ef2d83e88b1f2b5dd0ac6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda \\geq \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\ : \\ \\lambda \\neq \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"154\" height=\"43\" />, ignoring the case on equality.\n</p><p><b>Proof of Lemma 1:</b>\n</p><p>An optimal play is that every odd turn, Alice chooses 0. Assume turn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/3/1a304470cea606343537b74b23b336101730ae43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />. Bazza must satisfy:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d1138e0522a7d7b19c12f1c9f59f97e67bb11c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_2^2 + x_4^2 + \\dots + x_{2n}^2 \\leq 2k\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>By Cauchy-Schwarz,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/0/650a908e726416649e96dcaddc29710c6d10768a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_2 + x_4 + \\dots + x_{2k} \\leq \\sqrt{2}k\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Hence on Alice's next turn,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2f325ff6c7486c151a1ac55b46e25ee28242ea2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_1+\\dots +x_{2k} \\leq \\sqrt{2} k\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>That is maximality. Now imagine that Bazza goes, and now it is Alice's turn. From here, it is required <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fcd490e8859c186c49fcfc389081f7eb833f1d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2} k \\leq \\lambda(2k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"24\" />. We ignore the equality case (will go over in Lemma 3), so assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/514f575d4c1549842d4e0fc0c9c415de07452a87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda &gt; \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"65\" height=\"43\" />. Following the strategy, there is always a way for Alice to maximize her next move, specifically, by choosing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef8c8bc3bb81d6b874903373d4a30d2d7cde373.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2k+1}&gt;\\sqrt{2k+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"23\" />, from which it is required <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/a/cda8c2f7334f1ecf3409a44a8fd9489cc463f5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2k+1}^2\\le 2k+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"119\" height=\"23\" />. However, Bazza would obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/2/9f25917fbb5c8dd97a63459f82d70bfae164aaf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2k+1}^2&gt;2k+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"119\" height=\"23\" />, which is illegal. Hence, Alice wins. We will go back to the equality case in a moment.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 2:</b> Bazza can win if  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51ce9eb395b600678b07e3bccee74e62d67d1961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; \\lambda &lt; \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"98\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p><b>Proof of Lemma 2:</b>\n</p><p>Firstly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b82faab40a890b61e20d5f8be71529ededce90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is given via the statement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/7/5d75d654f7a9c4d36f9aa116badff68ed0af0834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda \\in \\mathbb{R}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />. An optimal play for Bazza is to choose the maximal move. After Alice chooses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/3503e77b626b2a0db6ed8717c80dd84233f12a1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, it is required that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/90409b2840bd63c0105ad85d0290e2fb0344bcd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k+x_{2k+1}^2+x_{2k+2}^2  \\leq 2k+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"224\" height=\"23\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/6/8b69f700c11fd2e1b330a78685d04cd6451a329f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2k+2} \\leq \\sqrt{2-x_{2k+1}^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"159\" height=\"35\" />. Let Bazza choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/7/f975f88527616fdd2d794032e9299a1c392cf2b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2k+2} = \\sqrt{2-x_{2k+1}^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"159\" height=\"35\" />. On Alice's side, that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49ec51a9b07e22e76d0ab4597bb101a7c2f305d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2k+1}+\\sqrt{2-x_{2k+1}^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"157\" height=\"35\" />. Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3b2546286f00191f2ddb39a794697cf8d6a71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2k+1} = t \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/10670c5f45fbf9e1971ffc9a35b5c45baecf375a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t+\\sqrt{2-t^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"21\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/4850d5d7a9c42feed4d73745680404d4dfb12758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t \\leq \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"22\" /> to keep the fraction viable (as otherwise that implies Bazza has no viable moves and therefore loses, which is not allowed in this case). Therefore, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2dbc489253323dee246e750b0812dd89982b9b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq t \\leq \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"22\" />, we request the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/10670c5f45fbf9e1971ffc9a35b5c45baecf375a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t+\\sqrt{2-t^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"21\" />. This is easy to find via geometry, the figure formed is a quarter circle in the first quadrant with points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e7029c9162ce9a7899470c2a57deb67ed71f59fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt{2},0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"24\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/4656cd8d376ac4c098ef03126db40aa538d4641b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,\\sqrt{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"24\" />. So the minimum value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/a/5aa6b39a88836ef70f7b63bb4de61996e2444bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t+\\sqrt{2-t^2} \\geq \\sqrt{2} \\ : \\ 0 \\leq t \\leq \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"254\" height=\"22\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, hence the minimum value of the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/4/ab493fa290e6b7bda1d996b601ccdd5dcce80380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 + \\dots + x_{2k} \\leq k\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"169\" height=\"22\" />. Alice requires <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/e/e2ee872ee82a51b41472696036ab7c704ec8b222.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 + \\dots + x_{2k} \\leq \\lambda(2k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" />. That is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/0/c005f72dbd6f4453f0ae657139e996cc81a36762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\sqrt{2}  \\leq  \\lambda(2k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"24\" />. The smallest move that can be chosen from Alice is 0, and when she does so, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/0/c005f72dbd6f4453f0ae657139e996cc81a36762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\sqrt{2} \\leq \\lambda(2k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"24\" />. Alice wins in this case, so assume the contrary, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e91d2de33b461856e09d7b57e2aff8948499804.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\sqrt{2} &gt; \\lambda(2k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"24\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/850947b78796bf0e86eeb8330af4b9d35af2e15f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda &lt; \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"65\" height=\"43\" /> is when Bazza wins. \n</p><p><b>Lemma 3:</b> Neither wins at the equality case:\n</p><p><b>Proof of Lemma 3:</b>\n</p><p>We know that Bazza cannot win in that case from <b>Lemma 2</b>. Hence, we must show that Alice cannot win. This is quite trivial however. Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fcd490e8859c186c49fcfc389081f7eb833f1d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2} k \\leq \\lambda(2k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"24\" /> we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/984a49d89f819638d3f19a97435eeef4c976b615.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\sqrt{2} \\geq k\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"22\" /> which is an equality. But then, if Bazza attempts her strategy, Alice could just play 0 and the same equality hits over and over and over again. Similarly, Alice could play 0, but then Bazza could attempt her strategy, hitting equality over and over again. Because neither player can attempt to steal victory, it is evident that no one would win.\n</p><p><b>2025 IMO/5:</b>\n</p><p>Applying <b>Lemma's 1,2,3</b>,\n</p><p>\\begin{array}{c} \\boxed{\\begin{array}{c|c}0&lt;\\lambda&lt;\\frac1{\\sqrt2}&amp;\\text{Bazza wins}\\\\[2mm]\\lambda=\\frac1{\\sqrt2}&amp;\\text{Neither wins}\\\\[2mm]\\lambda&gt;\\frac1{\\sqrt2}&amp;\\text{Alice wins}\\end{array}} \\end{array}.\n</p><p>~Pinotation \n</p><p>Note: The motivation for Alice Winning is to show that no matter what she were to play she can manipulate Bazza's movement. In addition, if Bazza were to play maximally when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> were minimal then he fully restricts Alice's movement.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO\" title=\"2025 IMO\">2025 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competitions_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competitions resources\">Mathematics competitions resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO\" title=\"2025 IMO\">2025 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2025 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018022852\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 288/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9401/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.902      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.902      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:33004:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018022852 and revision id 291159. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}